    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "beac0887_999087cb",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kernel/fpu/init.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 178,
      "author": {
        "id": 1928805
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-26T02:43:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had originally created this patch with just arm64 in mind. But Todd commented as follows: https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/3292853/comment/7dee5f2c_e5fc7290/\n\nI assumed that he wanted it to be a generic GKI thing available for all architectures if needed.",
      "parentUuid": "3010558b_431ea3e1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 178,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 178,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "8c75bd2379a0794c76db15f50e2706a8c041ca7a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cac7b439_2aeeaa3e",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kernel/fpu/init.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 178,
      "author": {
        "id": 1869395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-26T18:17:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can\u0027t find previous @tkjos@google.com\u0027s comments on this topic but I\u0027ll loop him into this review. The current kernel design is that each architecture defines its own `arch_task_struct_size` (hence the naming). So the changes should be added to fit the current design.",
      "parentUuid": "beac0887_999087cb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 178,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 178,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "8c75bd2379a0794c76db15f50e2706a8c041ca7a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
