      "writtenOn": "2026-02-27T00:10:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right and this MAX doesn\u0027t have to be a Kconfig since it\u0027s always a constant in all GKI kernels. I don\u0027t see the point of this complication over a simple define. We don\u0027t need anything more than:\n\n```\n#define GKI_TASK_STRUCT_VENDOR_SIZE_MAX 512\n```",
      "parentUuid": "369807d9_44794c3d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 298,
        "startChar": 7,
